DESCRIPTION:Venue not yet confirmed. We're expecting to be at Myhal Centre
  (University of Toronto)\, but please check this page closer to the date f
 or the final location and room number.&#x20\;\n\nTopic: Canadian Council R
 ecords: Nothing but PDFs\, and Toronto\n\nMost Canadian municipalities pub
 lish their council record as PDFs\, sometimes scanned.\n\nA handful of Saa
 S vendors cover roughly 500 cities between them\; the rest are a long tail
  of one-off formats\, and then there's Toronto\, whose minutes are a breat
 h of fresh air.\n\nMike will show what it took to build a searchable recor
 d across both.\n\nSpeaker: Mike Nikles (he/him)\n\nMike is the solo develo
 per behind Civic Lens\, a searchable record of Canadian council meetings\,
  bylaws and municipal spending\, built from the cities' own documents and 
 traced back to source.\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n
 \n7:20-7:50 Presentation and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:00 Breakout groups
